@startuml
title POST /api/ai-agents-teams/run-under-grant/prepare + /send — channel-paid, grantor-owned run
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

participant "Channel service\n(gateway / mail bridge)" as Channel #C8E6DC
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "Continuation store\n(encrypted artifacts)" as Store #E8DACB
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6

group Phase 1 — prepare (deploys nothing)
Channel -> API : POST .../run-under-grant/prepare\n{grant_id, prompt, channel_context}
API -> Domain : prepare run under grant
Domain -> Chain : getGrant(grant_id)
alt no grant
Domain --> API : 404 {code: grant_not_found}
else revoked
Domain --> API : 403 {code: grant_revoked}
else channel_context does not match the grant's\nchannel or principal
Domain --> API : 422 {code: grant_principal_mismatch}
else advisory day counter already at cap
Domain --> API : 429 {code: grant_caps_exceeded}
else granted team has no durable (Workflow v2) manifest
Domain --> API : 422 {code: team_not_durable}\n(legacy GraphL output is never revealable)
else admissible
Domain -> Store : encrypted run request v3 (channel_context\ninside — never on the public ledger) +\ncontinuation revision-0
Domain --> API : RunUnderGrantResp { run: RunResp,\n  grant_id, agents_team (resolved FROM the grant) }
API --> Channel : PrepareResponse { response, token }
end
end

group Sign and send
Channel -> Channel : sign with the CHANNEL wallet\n(grantee and payer; the grantor owns the run)
Channel -> API : POST .../run-under-grant/send\n{ echo, signed, token }
API -> Domain : deploy signed run
Domain -> Chain : deploy beginDurableRunUnderGrant
note right of Chain #FFF0C7
One atomic join over runsCh + grantsCh:
signer == grantee, not revoked, team match,
UTC-epoch-day counter, then registration with
owner = grantor and grant_id. A resent
same-signed envelope re-registers
idempotently without a second cap unit.
end note
alt clause aborts
Chain --> Domain : deploy errored
Domain -> Chain : re-read the grant to classify honestly
Domain --> API : 404 grant_not_found / 403 grant_revoked /\n429 grant_caps_exceeded / 500 internal_error
else node refuses the deploy for funds
Domain --> API : 402 {code: deploy_unfunded}\n(top up the channel wallet)
else finality not observed in the window
Domain --> API : 504 {code: deploy_not_finalized}\n— the run may still land: poll GET /runs/{run_id}
else clause lands
Chain --> Domain : finalized
Domain -> Chain : verify registration: run_id, grant_id link,\nteam, created_at, revision 0, "running",\nall five hashes
Domain -> Domain : resume the durable kernel\n(the same pipeline as a plain run)
Domain --> API : run-state JSON readback
API --> Channel : 200 run-state JSON
end
end

note over Channel, Chain #FFF0C7
The transport after registration is UNCHANGED from a plain
run: poll GET /runs/{run_id}, reveal under the grant's
authority, command under its delegated classes. Correctness
never depends on this send call surviving.
end note
@enduml
